# Input
```astro
<!-- should generate diagnostics -->
<div class="flex grid"></div>
<div class="hover:flex hover:grid"></div>
<div class={"p-2 p-4"}></div>
<div class:list={clsx("flex grid")}></div>

```

# Diagnostics
```
invalid.astro:2:18 lint/nursery/noTailwindConflictingClasses ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

  ! The Tailwind CSS class grid sets the same CSS properties as flex.
  
    1 │ <!-- should generate diagnostics -->
  > 2 │ <div class="flex grid"></div>
      │                  ^^^^
    3 │ <div class="hover:flex hover:grid"></div>
    4 │ <div class={"p-2 p-4"}></div>
  
  i The other class is here.
  
    1 │ <!-- should generate diagnostics -->
  > 2 │ <div class="flex grid"></div>
      │             ^^^^
    3 │ <div class="hover:flex hover:grid"></div>
    4 │ <div class={"p-2 p-4"}></div>
  
  i Only one of these classes takes effect, so the other one does nothing.
  
  i Remove the class that you don't need.
  
  i This rule belongs to the nursery group, which means it is not yet stable and may change in the future. Visit https://biomejs.dev/linter/#nursery for more information.
  

